---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"What We Buy from Banks"} description={"Past-due, matured, and classified hotel loans: whole loans, participations, and hotels banks already own. Acquisition criteria and the situations we look at."}>
  <Hero eyebrow={"For banks"} title={"What we buy from banks."} lead={"Past-due, matured, and classified hotel loans, from single loans to small pools."} />
  <SectionNav section="banks" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Acquisition criteria</p><h2>What we buy.</h2>
        <p>That includes hotels a bank already carries as <a href="/glossary/#oreo">OREO</a>. For a small pool, a <a href="/glossary/#loan-tape">loan tape</a> is the place to start.</p></div>
      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>Loan status</dt><dd>Past due, non-accrual, matured, or in forbearance. Loans in foreclosure, receivership, or borrower bankruptcy are eligible.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Collateral</dt><dd>Hotels: limited-service, select-service, extended-stay, and full-service, branded or independent. We also review loans secured by multifamily and retail properties.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Lien position</dt><dd>First mortgages and first deeds of trust, with the related security interest in furniture, equipment, and accounts.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Interest acquired</dt><dd>Whole loans, participation interests, and hotels the bank already owns.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Guaranteed loans</dt><dd>We review government-guaranteed hotel loans and work within the agency's consent requirements for a sale.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Transaction size</dt><dd>Single loans and small pools.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Situations</p><h2>The hotel loans <em>we are asked to look at.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="grid3">
        <div><span class="mono">01</span><h3>Unfunded improvement plan</h3><p>The brand has required renovations the owner cannot pay for, and the franchise is at risk.</p></div>
        <div><span class="mono">02</span><h3>Franchise default</h3><p>The brand has issued a default or termination notice for unpaid fees or failed inspections.</p></div>
        <div><span class="mono">03</span><h3>Maturity default</h3><p>The hotel is operating, the loan has matured, and a refinance will not cover the balance.</p></div>
        <div><span class="mono">04</span><h3>Payment default</h3><p>Revenue has fallen below what the hotel needs to cover debt service.</p></div>
        <div><span class="mono">05</span><h3>Receivership</h3><p>A receiver is operating the hotel while the lender decides between selling the loan and foreclosure.</p></div>
        <div><span class="mono">06</span><h3>Closed or lender-owned hotel</h3><p>The hotel has gone dark, or the lender has taken title and wants to sell.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="wrap intro">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">How we look at a loan</p><h2>We underwrite the operation along with the real estate.</h2>
        <div class="body"><p>On a hotel loan, we price the loan with the franchise, the required renovations, and the unpaid taxes already accounted for.</p>
        <p>That means reading the loan file closely and looking at the hotel as a business: its performance against its competitive set, who manages it, and what a transfer would require. The questions we work through are set out on the <a class="more arrow" href="/underwriting/">underwriting page</a>.</p></div></div>
      <dl class="pillars">
        <div><dt>The franchise</dt><dd>Whether the flag survives a default, and whether the lender's rights with the brand pass to a buyer of the loan.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>The improvement plan</dt><dd>What the brand requires, what it costs, and who will fund it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>The operation</dt><dd>Staff, licenses, taxes, and bookings that have to continue without a gap.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Not sure it fits?</p><h2>A one-page summary is enough to find out.</h2>
        <p>Balance, status, the hotel's brand and room count, and any recent valuation. We reply with an indicative price, or tell you plainly that the loan is not for us. See <a class="more arrow" href="/banks/information-to-send/">what to send</a>.</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/glossary/#whole-loan">Whole loan <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#participation">Participation interest <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/library/franchise/">The franchise when a hotel loan is sold <span>Library</span></a></li><li><a href="/library/pip/">Pricing a hotel loan with an unfunded improvement plan <span>Library</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Discuss a hotel loan in confidence."} text={"A conversation and an indicative price carry no obligation to sell."} label={"Start a conversation"} />
</Base>
